00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  you're  [Applause]  clearly such a strong person but why did  you decide to join the military in the  first place oh that's a funny story um  i decided to join the military because i  have a  cousin  she was in the air force now you hear me  i said she  she was in the air force she was my role  model  i saw her in the uniform  i saw her going places all over and it  looked so glamorous and it looked like  you know in my eyes that  the military was the place to be and she  looked not just  she looked so stupid she looked  important  and i wanted to be like that  so  that's one of the reasons why i joined  once you got in it and you saw how it  really functioned and you got onto the  inside and you weren't just looking at  the outside how did you  find that women were treated so  i love the military i want to say that  first  i love the united states military but  actually being in um  we as women we go to the front line we  are in war  and we're not recognized there was times  in the beginning  when i first joined  i didn't even get a chance to do the job  that i was trained for  we don't even get recognized  outside the military we do every single  job every single job that the military  offers we do  is it true that you had an interesting  interaction with a veteran after you  returned home so not just on the front  lines but back at home oh yes  um my wife and i we were we pulled up to  the gas station and i have disabled  veteran plates  i have a wounded warrior sticker in my  front window  obviously a veteran looking vehicle  and um a gentleman was behind me  pumping gas  and he finished pumping his gas and  pulled in front  and he came to salute me and said um  you know make sure you tell your husband  that i said thank him for his service  in turn i turned to him  and i told him you know what thank you  for your service  and i'm the veteran  and what was his reaction in that moment  i think he was shocked and embarrassed  and he just drove off  i first got to know about wounded  warrior about 10 years ago  a friend of mine is a big participator  and it brought the project to my  attention  and  when i  see  the way your life has transformed with  them  this is so much more than a topical  association  it's like  they it seemed like they did  give you a door that you walked through  and on the other side of that door was a  life waiting for you  let me tell you  i can't do anything but when i think of  wounded warrior project  a smile  because um  just like you said wounded warrior  project is not just an organization yes  this is an organization that  empowers  women this organization  literally gave me my life back it didn't  give me my life back it actually  boosted and kicked forward  my life  um without wounded warrior project i  probably wouldn't be here  um when the work project gave me a  community  gave me family  when you're in the military  you gain a family  and sometimes being injured and getting  out of the military you kind of lose  those connections lose that family  and every single event i've ever been on  with the warrior project it's like going  to a family reunion and i have that  family again i have those connections it  gives you that camaraderie and  without wounded warrior project i know  myself and a lot of others wouldn't be  here  well i'm so glad that you are here donna  and  on international women's day  your fierceness your strength your life  choices your life attitude choosing to  go and serve and protect choosing to be  on a high road when every other option  seems probably easier  you're such an inspiration thank you and  i'm so glad to meet you and hear your  story thank you donna thank you and to  learn more about how wounded warrior  project is helping lift up female  veterans visit wounded  woundedwarriorproject.org forward slash  empower women vets  thank you donna  [Music]

